flowchart TD
    Up["interface goes up<br/><b>does:</b> enables IPv6 device state and joins solicited-node multicast<br/><b>why next:</b> link-local address is required before routers/neighbors<br/><b>state:</b> tentative IPv6 configuration"]
    LL["link-local address<br/><b>does:</b> derives fe80::/64 address from stable secret/MAC policy<br/><b>why next:</b> address must pass DAD before use<br/><b>state:</b> tentative link-local address"]
    DAD["Duplicate Address Detection<br/><b>does:</b> sends Neighbor Solicitation for own address<br/><b>why next:</b> duplicate means address cannot be assigned<br/><b>state:</b> preferred address or duplicate failure"]
    RA["Router Advertisement<br/><b>does:</b> provides prefixes plus A/M/O flags and default router info<br/><b>why next:</b> flags decide SLAAC vs DHCPv6 handoff<br/><b>state:</b> prefix lifetimes and router learned"]
    Flags{"RA flags/prefix<br/><b>does:</b> A=autonomous prefix, M=managed DHCPv6<br/><b>state:</b> chosen address configuration path"}
    SLAAC["SLAAC global address<br/><b>does:</b> combines prefix with stable/random interface ID<br/><b>why next:</b> global address also needs DAD<br/><b>state:</b> tentative global address"]
    DHCP["DHCPv6 client<br/><b>does:</b> asks server for address or other config when flags require<br/><b>why next:</b> assigned address/options feed IPv6 stack<br/><b>state:</b> managed address or DNS/options"]
    NDP["NDP usable<br/><b>does:</b> resolves neighbors and maintains reachability cache<br/><b>state:</b> IPv6 can send to local-link next hops"]

    Up --> LL --> DAD --> RA --> Flags
    Flags -->|A=1| SLAAC --> DAD
    Flags -->|M=1 or other config| DHCP --> NDP
    DAD -->|no duplicate| NDP
    DAD -->|duplicate| Up

    classDef init fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb
    classDef decision fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706
    classDef ready fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a
    class Up,LL,RA init
    class DAD,Flags decision
    class SLAAC,DHCP,NDP ready
